compiler-rt: backport the DONT_DEFINE_EPRINTF guard in builtins/eprintf.c (AMD 0bace190 defect)

Upstream llvm/llvm-project 2e9df860468425645dcd1b241c5dbf76c072e314,
"[compiler-rt][builtins] Add compiler flags to catch potential errors that can
lead to security vulnerabilities", wraps the whole __eprintf definition in
#ifndef DONT_DEFINE_EPRINTF ... #endif. The AMD tree already passes
-Werror=format-nonliteral -DDONT_DEFINE_EPRINTF (CompilerRTUtils.cmake:639, macOS
>= 10.7) but still compiles the body, where fprintf(stderr, format, ...) trips
-Wformat-nonliteral. Our just-built clang's new -Wmissing-format-attribute (in the
-Wformat-nonliteral group) makes that a hard error (run 38570967283, osx-arm64).

diff --git a/compiler-rt/lib/builtins/eprintf.c b/compiler-rt/lib/builtins/eprintf.c
index 89fb0e3..daf90b4 100644
--- a/compiler-rt/lib/builtins/eprintf.c
+++ b/compiler-rt/lib/builtins/eprintf.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 //
 // It should never be exported from a dylib, so it is marked
 // visibility hidden.
+#ifndef DONT_DEFINE_EPRINTF
 #ifndef _WIN32
 __attribute__((visibility("hidden")))
 #endif
@@ -25,3 +26,4 @@ __eprintf(const char *format, const char *assertion_expression,
   fflush(stderr);
   compilerrt_abort();
 }
+#endif
